# Multi-plane spike: 2 Coders + middle + portal + Keycloak

Validates **plane branching**: mint and open apps on the correct control plane.
Alice has workspaces on **A and B**; Bob only on **B**.

## Architecture

```text
Keycloak (:8080)
    │  IdP JWT
Portal (:5173) ──► Middle (:8081) ──► Coder A (:3000)   alice-a
                      │            └► Coder B (:3001)   alice-b, bob-b
                      │
                      └─ GET /v1/workspaces/{id}/coder-app/{slug}?plane=a|b
                           → Set-Cookie coder_session_token (host-only) + 302 to
                             http://127.0.0.1:PORT/@user/ws/apps/slug/  (no token in URL)
```

Apps are **path-based** (`subdomain = false`): **ttyd** (terminal) + **code-server**.

For what it takes to open **`subdomain = true`** apps the same way (wildcard URL, cookie vs query token), see [`../docs/open-coder-apps-path-vs-subdomain.md`](../docs/open-coder-apps-path-vs-subdomain.md).
Built-in Coder web terminal is disabled (`display_apps.web_terminal = false`).

