**1. Coder client** (`coder.go`):

```go
type externalAuthStatus struct {
    Authenticated bool   `json:"authenticated"`
    ProviderID    string `json:"provider_id"`
    ValidateError string `json:"validate_error,omitempty"`
}

func (c *CoderClient) ExternalAuth(ctx context.Context, userToken, providerID string) (*externalAuthStatus, error) {
    var out externalAuthStatus
    path := "/api/v2/external-auth/" + url.PathEscape(providerID)
    if err := c.do(ctx, http.MethodGet, path, userToken, nil, &out); err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }
    return &out, nil
}
```

**2. Middle handler** (`planes.go` / `external_auth.go`) — check happens **here**:

```go
// GET /v1/external-auth/{id}?plane=a
func (s *Service) handleExternalAuthStatus(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    email, err := s.emailFromRequest(r)
    if err != nil {
        http.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusUnauthorized)
        return
    }
    providerID := r.PathValue("id") // e.g. "primary-gitlab"
    p, err := s.plane(r.URL.Query().Get("plane"))
    if err != nil {
        http.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusBadRequest)
        return
    }
    tok, err := s.ensureCoderTokenOnPlane(r.Context(), email, p.ID)
    if err != nil {
        http.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusBadGateway)
        return
    }
    st, err := p.Client.ExternalAuth(r.Context(), tok, providerID)
    if err != nil {
        http.Error(w, err.Error(), http.StatusBadGateway)
        return
    }
    // Ensure cookie so a follow-up window.open(auth_url) is already authenticated.
    http.SetCookie(w, &http.Cookie{
        Name:     "coder_session_token",
        Value:    tok,
        Path:     "/",
        HttpOnly: true,
        SameSite: http.SameSiteLaxMode,
        MaxAge:   int((2 * time.Hour).Seconds()),
    })
    writeJSON(w, http.StatusOK, map[string]any{
        "provider_id":   providerID,
        "authenticated": st.Authenticated,
        "plane_id":      p.ID,
        // Portal opens this only when authenticated == false
        "auth_url": p.URL + "/external-auth/" + url.PathEscape(providerID),
    })
}
```

**3. Register route** (`main.go`):

```go
mux.Handle("GET /v1/external-auth/{id}",
    svc.requireAuth(http.HandlerFunc(svc.handleExternalAuthStatus)))
```

**4. Portal** (`app.js`) — only consumes middle JSON:

```js
async function ensureGitLabLinked(planeId, providerId = "primary-gitlab") {
  await ensureAppSession(); // middle_session for top-level nav if needed
  const q = planeId ? `?plane=${encodeURIComponent(planeId)}` : "";
  const st = await api(`/v1/external-auth/${encodeURIComponent(providerId)}${q}`);
  if (st.authenticated) return true;
  // Middle already set coder_session_token on this host; open Coder consent page.
  window.open(st.auth_url, "_blank", "noopener,noreferrer");
  return false; // caller may poll / show "Connect GitLab then Refresh"
}

// Example: before create, or a "Connect GitLab" button
// if (!(await ensureGitLabLinked(ws.plane_id))) { alert("Complete GitLab login, then retry"); }
```

Optional poll after the popup:

```js
async function waitUntilGitLabLinked(planeId, providerId = "primary-gitlab", attempts = 30) {
  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
    const q = planeId ? `?plane=${encodeURIComponent(planeId)}` : "";
    const st = await api(`/v1/external-auth/${encodeURIComponent(providerId)}${q}`);
    if (st.authenticated) return true;
    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 2000));
  }
  return false;
}
```

### Inside the workspace

```bash
coder external-auth access-token primary-gitlab
# exit 0 → token on stdout (OK)
# exit 1 → not linked; stdout is the auth URL to open
```

### Alternatives (not implemented in this lab)

| Approach | When |
| --- | --- |
| **B. Portal owns GitLab OAuth** | Portal runs auth-code flow and injects the token into the workspace (env/secret). No Coder External Auth UI at all. |
| **C. Non-user tokens** | Deploy / project / group tokens — no interactive consent. |

There is no way to finish OAuth **from Terraform alone** with no browser hop; the consent
step needs a user agent. The hop should be **portal → Coder external-auth URL** (after
cookie), not “click Login with GitLab on the Coder dashboard.”

## Middle API (multi-plane)

| Endpoint | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `GET /v1/planes` | Configured plane ids + URLs |
| `GET /v1/workspaces` | Fan-out; each item has `plane_id`, `plane_url` |
| `POST /v1/workspaces` | Body may include `plane_id` |
| `GET /v1/workspaces/{id}/access?plane=` | Access choices for that plane |
| `GET /v1/workspaces/{id}/coder-app/{slug}?plane=` | Host-only cookie + 302 to clean app URL |
| `POST /v1/logout` | Clears `middle_session` + `coder_session_token` |

